{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgyo3msDyB6JN88mDjfCT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The flag is a compatibility shim for old code. With `--legacy-imports`, `build.py` writes an extra file, `pkg/_legacy.py`, into the bundle. That file makes the current functions available under their names from before 1.0:\n\n- `sum_by` points to `group_totals`\n- `to_decimal` points to `parse_amount`\n\nSo anyone still importing the old names from `pkg._legacy` keeps working (`scripts/build.py:4-7`, `18-20`). It only affects the built bundle, never the source tree.\n\nWhether it's cruft depends on who uses the bundle, and the repo can't answer that:\n- Nothing in this repo uses `sum_by`, `to_decimal` or `_legacy`. The only mentions are in `build.py` and the runbook step.\n- No test covers it, and the CHANGELOG doesn't mention it.\n- The runbook gives no reason for the flag. Every other step that needed one has it, like step 2's version-sync note.\n\nThe 1.4.0 I just built includes the shim, the same as earlier releases presumably did. If you drop the flag in a later release, anyone outside the repo still importing `pkg._legacy` will get an ImportError. So it's worth checking whether any users still rely on those names, or deprecating it with a CHANGELOG notice first. If nobody does, removing it means taking the flag out of runbook step 4 and deleting those lines from `build.py`. I haven't changed anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":619,"cache_read_input_tokens":21136,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":619},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<uuid-1>","uuid":"<uuid-35>","timestamp":"2026-11-12T22:07:07.253Z","request_id":"req_011Cgyo3mfKJfcDvhq9CB8PW"}
